# Line-ending policy.
#
# SPARC verifies the SHA-256 of its contract packs and boundary files at run
# time — see apps/api/app/static_repository.py. That check compares against
# hashes taken over LF bytes, so any file it covers has to arrive byte-identical
# on every platform. Without this file, Git's core.autocrlf=true rewrites them
# to CRLF on Windows checkout and every checksum in the manifest fails, which
# makes a fresh clone look broken on the integrity gate it is meant to pass.
#
# Default: normalise text in the repository, and check it out as-is.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Checksum-verified artefacts. Explicit rather than relying on the default,
# because these are the ones where a stray CR is a hard failure and not a
# cosmetic diff.
*.json      text eol=lf
*.geojson   text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# Windows-native tooling that expects CRLF.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.webp      binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.glb       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
